5. TECHNOLOGY STACK

Use the following architecture unless a documented technical limitation requires a change.

Frontend

- Next.js using the App Router.
- React.
- TypeScript with strict type checking.
- Tailwind CSS.
- Accessible, reusable UI components.
- Server Components by default.
- Client Components only where interactivity requires them.

Backend

Use Next.js server-side capabilities for application business logic.

Implement:

- Server Actions where appropriate.
- Route Handlers for HTTP APIs and integrations.
- Server-only database access.
- Centralized validation.
- Centralized authorization.
- Structured error handling.
- Transactional business operations.

Keep frontend presentation separate from business logic, data access, and security enforcement.

Database

- MySQL.
- Prisma ORM.
- Version-controlled database migrations.
- Explicit relational constraints.
- Appropriate database indexes.
- Transactional updates for important business operations.

Validation and forms

- Zod for input validation.
- React Hook Form where complex client-side form handling justifies it.
- Server-side validation for every untrusted request.

Client-side validation must never replace server-side validation.

Authentication

Use secure, server-side administrative authentication.

Prefer a maintained authentication solution compatible with Next.js, Prisma, and the chosen deployment environment.

If a custom credential-based authentication system is necessary, implement it carefully and document the security decisions.

Use Argon2id or an appropriately configured modern password-hashing algorithm.

File storage

Use a private or appropriately access-controlled object storage service for private customer uploads and sensitive business documents.

Use a compatible image storage service or object storage configuration for public product images.

Do not depend on local application filesystems for permanent uploads in serverless production environments.

Testing

Use appropriate tools for:

- Unit testing.
- API integration testing.
- Database integration testing.
- Component testing.
- End-to-end testing.
- Authentication and authorization testing.

AI

Use the official Google GenAI SDK or another explicitly selected supported provider SDK for server-side AI integration.

Never expose provider API keys in client-side code.

Do not make AI features dependent on fabricated responses presented as real AI output.

Package management

Use npm unless the existing environment or project constraints justify another package manager.

Keep dependencies minimal and explain why important dependencies exist.

Before installing packages, verify compatibility with the selected Next.js and React versions.

Do not use deprecated packages when maintained alternatives are available.

